ng they've been  singing there for repeal  they have no replace President Trump  confirmed that he will hold Americans  hostage through the 2020 election when  it comes to health care  he promises reelect me and maybe you can  take a peek at my back-up plan after  that which they don't have what a ruse  what a shame what a disgrace we know  that what the Republicans health care  plan might look like gut protections for  Americans with pre-existing conditions  massive losses of coverage destabilize  insurance markets help the big fat  insurance companies the drug companies  and all their special interest wealthy  donors so when President Trump insists  he has a magic plan that we can see if  only the American people reelect him we  know is just not true the American  people will not stand for the president  playing cynical games with health care  and politically by betting with the  health of twenty thirty forty million  Americans  he is sure to lose don't let president  Trump fool you America Republicans are  not the party of health care they are  the party that wants to end your health  care we Democrats will not stop fighting  tooth and nail to protect Americans  health care today tomorrow and on in  through 2021  Pelosi good morning everyone it's an  honor to join the distinguished  Democratic leader of the United States  Senate senator Shaheen a leader on the  protecting the care of the American  people and Colin Allred from the House  of Representative freshman member who's  taken the lead on this issue from day  one in the Congress we're here to  condemn what the president did last week  the Trump administration radically  expanded its war on the Affordable Care  Act on Americans health care asking the  court to strike down every last  provision of the ACA  the distinguished leader went through  some of the concerns some bear repeating  imagine that he would say after the  Republicans misrepresented their  position on pre-existing conditions  remember during the campaign they said  all we're for the benefit of not having  pre-existing condition be a barrier to  your access to health care they said  that in spite of the fact that over and  over again they have had voted to  eliminate that benefit and now the  president is acting in a way to not only  eliminate that benefit which is so  important also to eliminate a companion  benefit that goes with a pre-existing  condition to eliminate the ban on  lifetime limits and annual limits on  people with who need health care this is  terrible being a woman no longer a  pre-existing condition under the ACA up  to 26 years of age you can be on your  parents policy lengthening the stability  and the solvency of Medicare hail care  they think Medicare should wither on the  vine that is the Republican mantra when  Medicare was passed they said it would  lead to a socialist dictatorship they do  not believe in a public role they are  anti governance so this is not an issues  fight or legislative fight it's a values  fight for our country that we value the  health  wellbeing of the American people and we  recognize that their financial stability  is related to their health stability the  the Medicaid expansion as the  distinguished chairman Lee Durr said  this isn't just about the 20 million  people who have now have access to  quality affordable health care it's  about over 150 million families who have  better care better benefits again no  lifetime limits no pre-existing  condition ban and some of the other  provisions that I mentioned better  benefits lowering the increase in cost  improving the health not just the health  care but the good health of America is  about prevention it's about nutrition  it's about so many things that perhaps  they don't understand  but what we do understand is they do not  believe in public policy that affects  the good health of the American people  and that is why we are going to have  this resolution debated on the floor  today vote it tomorrow  from day one congressman Collin already  freshman from Texas led the way House  Democrats voted to throw the full legal  weight of the Democrats in the House of  Representatives and we hope that some  Republicans will join us against the  Texas lawsuit he's from Texas but more  than 190 Republicans voted to being  fully complicit in everything that this  monstrous proposal puts forth so now  because of president Trump's actions  which are to be condemned that lawsuit  is that lawsuit is even more dangerous  than it was in January and that is why  we were bringing forth the Allred  resolution this week the American people  deserve to know exactly where their  representatives stand on the Trump  administration's vicious campaign to  take away their health care this is so  interesting because the president has  been trying to do away with the  Affordable Care Act from day one we know  that and the way it was protected was  not just by our inside maneuvering it  was because of the outside mono a  mobilization of so many groups many who  are present here today  10,000 events they had 10,000 and  alzheimer 10,000 events around the  country  the little lobbyists the patient  advocacy groups age can protect our care  all kinds of organizations and  individuals coming forth with the power  of their individual stories I wasn't  just about statistics as compelling as  they are it was about the individual  stories and the individual stories of  little children born with a pre-existing  condition whose families need everything  their they need they need the health  care but they need Medicare Medicaid as  well there are children with a  pre-existing condition the president is  saying to them you now have a lifetime  limit on the care you the insurance you  can receive saying to little children  your pre-existing condition is going to  ban you from having health care that is  affordable you can have health care but  this cost will go through the roof  that's what the president is s