ts 45 Democrats to  independence to introduce a resolution  that calls on the Department of Justice  to reverse its position in the Texas v  United States lawsuit more than 20  million of our family members friends  and neighbors across the country have  gained access to health care coverage  that they need and deserve through the  Affordable Care Act already 7 million of  them have lost access to health  insurance because of the actions of this  Trump administration and if the law is  overturned those living with  pre-existing conditions stand to lose  the most children like Bodhi from  Concord a young boy who lives with  spinal muscular atrophy it's a disease  that affects his mobility and that costs  hundreds of thousands of dollars a year  and necessary medication to keep him  alive well if the Trump administration  has its way millions like Bodhi could be  denied insurance coverage because of  their disease insurers will be able to  jack up costs or even cut  coverage after medical bills reach an  arbitrary threshold repealing the ACA  and unraveling the progress that we've  made is reckless we know we need to do  things to make the law work better but  as policymakers our job is to fix laws  to work better for everyone now there  are a lot of reasons why we should work  together to fix our health care system  more than 20 million reasons and they  live in Republican and Democratic  districts throughout the country and  it's their health care that's at stake  but for that we need Republicans our  Republican colleagues to come to the  table and to defend their constituents  instead of the president ensuring the  health and safety of the American people  should transcend politics so I say this  to Senate and House Republicans you have  a choice you can sit idly by while the  president strips your constituents of  their health care or you can work with  us to protect Americans care and improve  the system now I'd like to introduce  representative Colin already fro